WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Let me show you a handy tool: Google Cloud Shell.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.966
To start up cloud shell click on the terminal icon in Google Cloud Console.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.000
At the bottom of your screen a terminal appears.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.200
This terminal is connected to a small temporary Linux VM

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.500
You can use this terminal to do normal management tasks like

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.000
creating VMs or storage buckets, building Docker images, or accessing

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.900
your Cloud SQL DB.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:25.900
The VM that is created has most of the tools you need to work on your application

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:28.900
including text editors

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.900
and compliers or interpreters for Go, Java, Python, Ruby, and Node.js

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.000
I find Cloud Shell to be especially helpful when I'm on the road.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Hotel and conference wifi can be spotty but my Cloud Shell instance

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.500
is sitting in a Google data center so it is great for doing the heavy handed tasks

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.000
involved in managing my projects.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.800
I hope you try out Cloud Shell soon.

